    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. The build succeeds with `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` (AcceptanceTest is the only test class in the project).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `timezone` field derived from the owner's locality/region via the fixed region-to-timezone table.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `timezone` string property to the `Owner` schema (which generates `OwnerDto`), documenting the mapping `NSW->Australia/Sydney, VIC->Australia/Melbourne, QLD->Australia/Brisbane`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added `@Mapping(target = \"timezone\", expression = \"java(timezone(owner))\")` and a `timezone(owner)` default method that reuses the existing `locality(owner)` derivation and maps the region code to its IANA timezone name, returning `null` for regions outside the table.\n\nThe approach follows the existing pattern in the mapper (each derived field has a `@Mapping` expression backed by a `default` method) and layers cleanly on top of the already-present `locality` derivation, so `NSW` \u2192 `Australia/Sydney` as the acceptance test expects.",
